    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32542" root="غنى" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَنًى</span></b> , (K, TA,) with fet-h, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْصُور</span>, (TA,)
<i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَئِنَّةٌ</span>; so in the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكَانُ كَذَا غَنًى مِنْ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٍ</span> [<i>Such a place is meet, fit,</i> or <i>proper, for
such a one;</i> as though meaning a place of freedom
from want]; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْهُ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْنًى</span></b> . (K, TA.)

